KONOHAGAKURE — SHARINGAN USE POLICY
CLASSIFICATION: Sensitive.

The Sharingan is a kekkei genkai dojutsu of the Uchiha clan and a strategic asset of the village. Its ability to copy techniques, perceive chakra, and cast genjutsu makes it both invaluable and coveted by rival villages.

Provisions:
- Sharingan bearers are cautioned against unnecessary display; the eye is a target for theft (transplant) by enemies.
- Non-Uchiha bearers of an implanted Sharingan (e.g., Hatake Kakashi) keep the eye covered when not in use to conserve chakra and avoid drawing attention.
- Copied techniques belonging to allied shinobi are used with discretion.
- The village protects the secret of the Sharingan's higher forms as classified knowledge.

Loss or theft of a Sharingan is a critical security incident to be reported to the Hokage's office at once.
Issued under Council authority.
